{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg84jdvQDsrrthvckHyt6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three rows changed meaning, and I blessed and re-anchored all three. Two commits, each ending `WI: WI-931`, and the commit checks passed on both:\n\n| Commit | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `5b01e23a7` | The verdict under `## amendment`: `VERDICT: MEANING rows=3`, then `SITTING: JUDGED kinds=amendment`. The kit's parser accepts it under the combined binding. |\n| `dfa037efa` | `snapshot --reattests SR-238,LLR-026,TC-026`. All three registries were copied, and no other drifted row blocked it. |\n\n**Why meaning:** the rows remove guards, so the guaranteed scope shrinks:\n- **SR-238:** the tree-kill guarantee now runs only while the coordinator supervises a launched session. A process that joins the Windows job mid-kill is terminated but may still be ending for milliseconds. Two sub-second windows are named as outside the guarantee: an interruption during launch, and that late joiner.\n- **LLR-026:** it drops the \"close the job before the snapshot\" step and launch-window ownership. Its error is now \"the named tree-end error\" rather than the class name, which the naming rule bars from row text.\n- **TC-026:** it drops exactly the six tests for the removed guards and names the seven kept ones, all of which exist.\n\n**Why blessed:** the owner ruled these guards not worth their cost (D-011, from the contrived-guards audit), and the new text states its limits honestly. Everything kept still holds:\n- containment, and refusal of a child that can't be contained;\n- the terminate, the member snapshot and the wait before it;\n- the raise for a member the kill can't open;\n- the 10 s bound;\n- ending the tree on a deadline or an interruption during supervision.\n\n**The risk I checked:** the tree-end error stops being a `BaseException` and becomes an ordinary `OSError`, which an ordinary handler could swallow. It still stops the coordinator:\n- `run_session` converts only launch errors, and the tree kill runs in its supervision `finally`, outside that conversion.\n- `act` re-raises everything.\n- Keep-warm catches the error by name.\n- The `except OSError` handlers in `agent_loop` and `dispatch` only wrap file reads.\n\n**Advisory:** LLR-026 no longer says the tree-end error must never be turned into a session result. Today that holds only because of how the code is structured. SR-238 still forbids continuing, but a future broad `except OSError` around a launch would breach it without the LLR saying why. A later edit could restate that without naming a carrier.\n\nThe untracked `003-ADJUDICATE-4dbd3bd.md.requested` belongs to the coordinator, and I didn't touch it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":855,"cache_read_input_tokens":708185,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":855},"output_tokens":720,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73ae5cf9-d335-4bb7-a08f-7631da597f26","uuid":"e64a2fde-3867-4ce8-9d67-454e8952fc08","timestamp":"2026-10-17T15:43:12.048Z","request_id":"req_011Cg84jdeHRMHCJCx6Ae23j"}
